.key OUT/A
; The same steps for whichever stack is bsdsocket.library (unit 0, 10.0.3.15).
FailAt 30
Copy SHARED:bench/curl SHARED:bench/netprof RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:curl +rwed QUIET
Protect RAM:netprof +rwed QUIET
Version bsdsocket.library >SHARED:bench/<OUT>
Echo "== curl https example.com" >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
RAM:curl -s -S -o NIL: -w "%{http_code} %{size_download} verify=%{ssl_verify_result} %{time_total}s*N" https://example.com/ >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
Echo "== curl http 16 MB from the PC" >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
RAM:curl -s -S -o RAM:big.bin -w "%{http_code} %{size_download} %{speed_download}B/s %{time_total}s*N" http://10.0.3.2:8000/big.bin >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
Echo "== curl https 20 MB (speed.cloudflare.com)" >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
RAM:curl -s -S -o NIL: -w "%{http_code} %{size_download} %{speed_download}B/s %{time_total}s verify=%{ssl_verify_result}*N" "https://speed.cloudflare.com/__down?bytes=20000000" >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
Echo "== netprof 32 MB" >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
RAM:netprof recv 10.0.3.2 mb=32 quiet >RAM:np.log
RAM:netprof send 10.0.3.2 mb=32 quiet >>RAM:np.log
Search RAM:np.log "Throughput" >>SHARED:bench/<OUT>
Delete RAM:big.bin QUIET
